34	    void on_page_message(const std::string& text);
35	
36	    // `added` names a printer the conversation just added: this one push
37	    // leads the printers list with it and asks the page to highlight it.
38	    void push_state(const std::string& added = {});
39	    // The live path, for a screen that stays up while its printers change
40	    // under it: re-reads only the printers, and sends the whole state only
41	    // when a card would look different from the last state sent. The printer
42	    // the last push_state named keeps its place and its highlight, so a live
43	    // push never reorders the column or cuts the highlight short. Projects
44	    // are re-read with any send; nothing that changes them alone happens
45	    // while Home is on screen, except a projects folder that could not be
46	    // read becoming readable: while the page shows that problem, the
47	    // projects are re-read on every refresh too. Returns whether it sent.
48	    bool refresh_if_changed();
