content.text:
Stage 3 is committed on `claude/gcode-print-history` and there is no PR, so nothing needed closing. I've sent you 11 screenshots, all taken from harness runs that passed with 0 failures.

**Commits.** Stage 3 is `49f8ecd0c5` ("Print a recorded G-code again from the file the project kept"), on top of stages 1 and 2. After it I added `2cd1aac1dc`, a test-only commit that makes the harness take the extra pictures below. The worktree is clean.

**Branch.** It is local only. `gh` isn't installed on this machine, but origin has no branch by this name, and a PR can't exist without one.

**Screenshots.** They come from three harness runs, all on the fake Bambu printer with isolated data folders. All of them are in `C:\b\gph-review`.
- **Ways in:**
  - the chat marker with its "history" link;
  - the project pane's single row ("3 G-codes · last finished Sep 12");
  - a project that never printed;
  - Home, showing the header link, the project card's line and the printer card's line ("2 prints · last finished today").
- **The screen:**
  - opened from the project with its filter, showing Print again and Export…;
  - unfiltered, opened from Home;
  - an export edited by hand, showing "changed outside JusPrin" and Export again.
- **Print again:**
  - OrcaSlicer's Select Machine dialog opened from the kept package, with the picture, time, weight and filament read from that file;
  - the entry after the reprint, with a third "Sent to" row;
  - the kept package altered on disk: Print again is withheld and an orange "Kept file changed on disk" note appears;
  - the kept copy deleted: Print again and Export… are both withheld, with "File no longer kept · slice again to print it".

**Things to look at when you review:**
- **Filament warning in Select Machine.** The dialog shows an orange "external filament is unknown" warning. That comes from the fake printer, whose external spool reports no filament; it isn't caused by this change.
- **No print row for the reprint.** The reprint doesn't add a Printing or Finished row because the fake printer was left in its "failed" state, so it never reported starting the reprint.
- **The entry's name changes after Export again.** The name follows the most recent export, so after Export again it reads "… (2).gcode". That's the stage 2 naming rule ("the exported file, else the plate").
- **The project card still says "Sent Oct 28" after a finished print.** That status line is stage 1 logic, and the second send was later than the finish.
- **The printer card's history line only shows when the card is open.** An idle printer starts folded as a one-line chip, and the chip has no history line.
